# Corpus unit lbcs/C05 — gap (comparative claim short of the variance bar)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/lbcs.yaml C05 (comparative, controlled_comparison; corpus pin 62e9b54;
# claim_type adjudicated via double annotation 2026-07-22). Headline: at ImageNet-1k, LBCS has
# the highest Top-5 accuracy among {Uniform, EL2N, GraNd, Moderate, CCS, Probabilistic, LBCS}
# at each predefined ratio, and its optimized ratio falls below the predefined ratio
# (68.53 < 70, 77.82 < 80) (E05, Table 4).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Nearest-competitor convention: the annotation argmaxes Top-5 over a seven-method set; the
#     unit's formal atom takes the nearest mask-based competitor, Probabilistic, as B (the
#     grouping trick is applied to both LBCS and Probabilistic, so it is the binding comparison).
#     The rest of the method set stays in nl and the leaf refs.
#   * Bundled conjunctive claim: the binding conjunct is (a) the Top-5 argmax; the arithmetic
#     ratio-reduction conjunct (b) 68.53 < 70 and 77.82 < 80 lives in nl and refs
#     (LOWERING §Formal atoms, bundled claims).
#   * The mandatory variance_reported CQ has no discharging leaf: E05 metrics list Top-5 and
#     optimized ratio with no repetition count or std (unlike E01's explicit 10-run mean+-std),
#     so the Top-5 margins may be within run-to-run noise. An open mandatory obligation is an
#     IncompleteArgument rejection, so no complete controlled_comparison is declarable — E2-
#     style gap on empty complete support (adaptive-pruning/C03 pattern). baseline_parity
#     (identical ResNet-50/SGD post-selection training) and measurement_validity (grouping trick
#     applied symmetrically; Top-5 a standard metric) are annotated met and kept as leaves.
#   * The optional "all baselines present at ImageNet scale" CQ is unmet (Influential absent),
#     so scope_match is not discharged; it has no status effect and is noted here only.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact lbcs at sha256:0cc27415e6b1
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------------------

claim c05
  nl      = "At ImageNet-1k, LBCS attains the highest Top-5 accuracy among {{Uniform, EL2N, GraNd, Moderate, CCS, Probabilistic, LBCS}} at each predefined ratio, and its optimized selection ratio falls below the predefined one (68.53 vs 70, 77.82 vs 80)"
  formal  = better(lbcs, probabilistic, top5_accuracy, imagenet1k)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = reviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: E05's Top-5 argmax cells at both ratios plus the optimized-ratio cells,
# per result cell, folded into refs.
leaf e1 : reports(e05, compares(lbcs, probabilistic, top5_accuracy, imagenet1k, favorable))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E05, Table-4, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N11]

leaf e2 : matched_setup(lbcs, probabilistic, e05)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E05-Procedure-steps-2-4, logic/experiments.md#E05-Setup]

leaf e3 : valid_measurement(top5_accuracy, e05)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E05-Procedure-step-2, logic/experiments.md#E05-Setup]

# --- ... but no complete argument is declarable -------------------------------------------------

# (Intentionally no `arg`: variance_reported(e05) has no honest leaf — E05 reports no repetition
# count or std at ImageNet scale — and corpus-v1 makes that obligation mandatory. The claim's
# complete-support set is therefore empty.)

status c05

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: no arguments.
# Claim status:
#   c05 -> gap (empty complete support; statusC = Gap iff null claimSupport, spec §8)
